# kk: Skip provably passing UBO bounds checks in compute dispatches
# https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/46466 state=opened
# ### What does this MR do and why?

<!--Describe in detail what your merge request does and why.-->

```
kk: Skip provably passing UBO bounds checks in compute dispatches

With robust buffer access, a UBO read at a constant offset is lowered to
load_global_constant_bounded, which checks the offset against the size
field of the buffer's descriptor on every invocation.  When the
descriptor is already bound at dispatch time, that check can be decided
on the CPU instead.

For each compute shader, record every such read whose descriptor sits at
a constant offset in a set whose address comes from the root table,
keeping the largest offset per descriptor, and generate a second MSL
variant in which those reads are plain load_global_constant_offset.  At
dispatch, read each recorded descriptor from the bound set (or push
descriptor data) and use the variant only when every size is larger
than its largest offset.  In that case each removed check would have
passed, so the variant performs the same reads as the checked shader.

The check is skipped, and the checked shader used, for sets whose layout
has UPDATE_AFTER_BIND or UPDATE_UNUSED_WHILE_PENDING bindings, since
their descriptors may change before execution, and for unbound sets.
Indirect and conditional dispatches use the same check.

The variant is compiled once, on first use, on a low-priority device
queue; until it is ready the checked pipeline is used.  The variant
source is stored with the shader binary, and the recorded entries are
validated when a binary is loaded.

MESA_KK_DEBUG=no_proof turns this off, and MESA_KK_DEBUG=sync_proof
compiles the variant inline on first use.

Assisted-by: LLM
