+/* Returns true when every UBO read listed in the shader's proof entries is in
+ * bounds for the descriptors bound now.
+ *
+ * The checked shader guards each such read with `offset < size`, where offset
+ * is a constant and size is read from the descriptor at execution time. When
+ * the descriptor's size is already larger than the largest offset, every one
+ * of those comparisons is true, so the shader without them performs exactly
+ * the same reads. This needs the descriptor memory to be the same at
+ * execution as it is now, which holds unless the layout allows updates after
+ * binding.
